|  - Structural Visual Diffing: SSIM change detection between actions    |
|  - Action Confirmation: Ensures UI state changed before next turn      |
+------------------------------------------------------------------------+
```

---

## 2. Core Capabilities

### A. Slicing Aided Hyper Inference (SAHI)
* Standard vision models resize images to $640\times640\text{ px}$, causing small UI elements, text, or distant objects to vanish into blur.
* SAHI partitions massive canvases (e.g. $3840\times2160$) into overlapping tiles with a defined stride, runs inference on each tile, and merges overlapping bounding boxes back into global coordinate space.

### B. Natural Language Visual Grounding
* Maps user directives (*"click the gear settings icon"*, *"find the cancel button"*) into standard normalized coordinates:
  $$\text{Box} = [y_{\min}, x_{\min}, y_{\max}, x_{\max}]$$
  with click centroid $(\bar{x}, \bar{y})$ in physical screen pixels.

### C. Multi-Scale Crop-and-Zoom Heuristics
* When confidence is borderline ($0.50 \le c \le 0.80$), automatically crops an expanded region of interest (ROI) centered around the target and performs a secondary high-zoom pass before executing clicks.

### D. Structural Visual Diffing (SSIM)
* Compares pre-action and post-action frames using Structural Similarity Index (SSIM) and perceptual hashing to verify that a click or keystroke actually caused the expected UI state mutation.

